  "G3v2_live_swaps_latency": {
   "note": "G3 with the brain's structural latency allowed for (brain-11 candidates only, frozen before any of them existed; G3 v1 is kept and reported). Same 9 logged Minus Two windows, same plant-validity filter and 3.5 m/s check. The speed at +1 s must lie within 0.5 m/s of the band between FastMotorPD and FastMotorPD with 80 ms of added command delay (the brain's measured 70-90 ms output lag behind its teacher), both in the same plant. Why: the PD with +80 ms is up to 0.555 m/s off the PD in these windows (gapon-01:16.1), so v1's 0.5 m/s tolerance is below the latency floor of any brain; a deviation away from both (e.g. over-braking in a capped arch turn where the delayed PD is faster) is not excused.",
